            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A mount assembly for use with a navigable tracker comprises a frame, a coupler, a coupler lock, a guide, an anchor and a guide lock. The frame defines a seat and a coupler seat. The coupler has a tracker interface for releasably securing to the navigable tracker, and a perch supported by the coupler seat for selective movement relative to the frame about a coupler point. The coupler lock is operatively attached to the frame and selectively operable between a secured configuration to restrict movement of the coupler relative to the frame, and a movable configuration to permit limited movement of the coupler relative to the frame about the coupler point. The guide defines a bore and is arranged in the seat for selective pivoting movement about a pivot point disposed within the bore. The anchor has a shank arranged for selective sliding engagement with the bore. The guide lock is coupled to the frame and selectively operable between a locked configuration to restrict movement of both the anchor and the guide relative to the frame, and a released configuration to simultaneously permit pivoting movement of the anchor relative to the frame about the pivot point and translational movement of the anchor relative to the guide through the bore.</p>
